💭 Fibonacci in Emojicode.
💭
💭 Same problem as the other five folders: read N, print fib(N) after an
💭 "N? " prompt. Emojicode is the only one of the six with a type system, so
💭 this is also the only one that can decline bad input politely instead of
💭 crashing, wrapping or looping forever.

🏁 🍇
  💭 👄 puts a string on standard output; 😀 is the same thing plus a newline.
  👄 🔤N? 🔤❗️

  💭 ▶️👂🏼 is an initializer on 🔡 that blocks until Enter. 🔧 trims it.
  🆕🔡▶️👂🏼❗️ ➡️ typed

  💭 🔢 returns 🍬🔢 — an optional integer — because the text might not be a
  💭 number at all. This is the conditional-unwrap form of ↪️: the block runs
  💭 only if there was a value, and n is that value.
  ↪️ 🔢 🔧 typed❗️ 10❗️ ➡️ n 🍇
    0 ➡️ 🖍🆕 a
    1 ➡️ 🖍🆕 b

    💭 Counting down with an explicit ▶️ 0 is also the guard for negative
    💭 input: the loop simply never runs, and a stays 0.
    n ➡️ 🖍🆕 countdown
    🔁 countdown ▶️ 0 🍇
      a ➕ b ➡️ sum
      b ➡️ 🖍 a
      sum ➡️ 🖍 b
      countdown ⬅️➖ 1
    🍉

    💭 🧲…🧲 interpolates, and converts the 🔢 to a 🔡 on the way in.
    😀 🔤🧲a🧲🔤❗️
  🍉
  🙅 🍇
    😀 🔤🤷 that was not a number.🔤❗️
    💭 🚪 on the 💻 type exits with a status code.
    🚪 🐇💻 1❗️
  🍉
🍉
